{
    "background_story": "Joy was a free-spirited artist who rejected the conventional norms of the art world. She refused to be tied down to a specific style or genre, instead embracing an unbranded approach to her craft. Her paintings were a fusion of abstract expressionism, street art, and folk art, making her a difficult artist to categorize. Joy's independence and nonconformity sparked both criticism and admiration from the art community. She turned down lucrative offers from galleries and collectors who wanted to mold her into a more marketable commodity. Instead, Joy chose to showcase her work in unconventional spaces, such as abandoned buildings and street corners. Her unbranded approach to art earned her a loyal following of fans who appreciated her authenticity and creative freedom.",
